    </div>

    <div role="tabpanel" id="page-guide" aria-labelledby="tab-page-guide" class="space-y-6" hidden>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-guide-reading" id="guide-reading">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-guide-reading">{{ icon('book-open') }}Reading the report</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="guide-text">This page explains each part of the report.</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="table guide-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>What it shows</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Dataset Overview</td><td>The number of rows and columns, the memory use, the duplicate rows, and the column types.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Alerts</td><td>Possible problems in the data, grouped by type.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Target</td><td>How closely each column links to the target, and how the target changes with the values of a column. This section appears when you set a target.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Variables</td><td>One row for each column, with its type, its missing values, and summary numbers. Click a heading to sort the rows. Click a column name to open its details.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Column Details</td><td>The statistics and a chart for one column. Choose the column in the list. A column with a Skewed alert has tabs above the chart. They show the values after log1p, after Yeo-Johnson, and without the zeros.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Correlations</td><td>How closely two columns change together. Each tab uses one method.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Interactions</td><td>A plot of one column against another column.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Missing Patterns</td><td>Groups of columns that are missing in the same rows. The Rows value counts the rows that have exactly that pattern.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Outliers</td><td>Values far from the other values in a numeric column. A value is an {{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outlier", "outlier") }} when it lies more than 1.5 times the {{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interquartile_range", "IQR") }} below the first quartile or above the third quartile. A {{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartile", "quartile") }} marks a quarter of the sorted values. The IQR is the distance between the first and the third quartile.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Sample</td><td>The first rows, the last rows, a random set of rows, the rows with the most missing values, and the duplicate rows of the data.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-guide-alerts" id="guide-alerts">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-guide-alerts">{{ icon('triangle-alert') }}Alerts</h2>
        {% set fes = 'https://feat.engineering/' %}
        {% set guide_alerts = [
          {
            'name': 'High Missing',
            'meaning': 'A column has many missing values.',
            'threshold': '> 5%',
            'limit': 'of the values are missing.',
            'fixes': [
              ['Value is absent by design, such as no garage', 'Fill it with None in a category column. Fill it with 0 in a count or an area column.'],
              ['Value exists but was not recorded', 'Impute it, for example with the median of a group. Fit the imputer on the train data only.'],
              ['Your model accepts missing values', 'Leave the gaps. Some tree models handle missing values without imputation.'],
              ['Gaps can carry meaning', 'Add a flag that marks the missing rows. For prediction, the pattern of gaps can help the model.'],
              ['Several columns are missing in the same rows', 'Open the Missing Patterns section. One cause can explain several columns at once.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kuhn and Johnson, chapter 8', fes ~ '08-Handling_Missing_Data.html'],
              ['Sperrin and others, 2020', 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclinepi.2020.03.028'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Constant',
            'meaning': 'A column has only one value.',
            'threshold': '≤ 1',
            'limit': 'distinct value.',
            'fixes': [
              ['Every row has the same value', 'Drop the column. A model cannot learn from a column that never changes.'],
              ['Every value is missing', 'The column is empty. Look at the data source, then drop the column.'],
              ['Your data is a filtered or small sample', 'Look at how you took the sample. Keep the column if it changes in the full data.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kuhn and Johnson, chapter 5', fes ~ '05-Encoding_Categorical_Predictors.html'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Constant Length',
            'meaning': 'Every value in a text column has the same length.',
            'threshold': 'min = max',
            'limit': 'for the length of the values.',
            'fixes': [],
            'sources': [],
          },
          {
            'name': 'High Cardinality',
            'meaning': 'Almost every value in a column is different. ' ~ ext('https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinality_(data_modeling)', 'Cardinality') ~ ' is the count of distinct values.',
            'threshold': '> 95%',
            'limit': 'of the values are distinct.',
            'fixes': [
              ['A real category with many levels, such as zip code', 'Use target encoding. It replaces each level with the average target value. Fit it on the train data with cross fitting, so the target does not leak.'],
              ['Rare levels hold few rows', 'Pool the rare levels into Other.'],
              ['You want fewer columns without using the target', 'Use feature hashing. It maps many levels to a fixed number of columns.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kuhn and Johnson, chapter 5', fes ~ '05-Encoding_Categorical_Predictors.html'],
              ['Micci-Barreca, 2001', 'https://doi.org/10.1145/507533.507538'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Duplicates',
            'meaning': 'Some rows appear more than once.',
            'threshold': 'any',
            'limit': 'duplicate row.',
            'fixes': [
              ['Copies are mistakes', 'Drop the extra copies before you split the data. A row in both the train set and the test set inflates the score.'],
              ['Near copies exist', 'Look for near duplicates too. They inflate the score in the same way.'],
              ['Repeats are real, such as repeat visits by one person', 'Keep them. Split by group, so that one person stays in one set.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kapoor and Narayanan, 2023', 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patter.2023.100804'],
              ['Barz and Denzler, 2020', 'https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.00423'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'High Zeros',
            'meaning': 'A numeric column has many zeros.',
            'threshold': '> 5%',
            'limit': 'of the values are zero.',
            'fixes': [],
            'sources': [],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Infinite Values',
            'meaning': 'A numeric column has values that are infinite.',
            'threshold': '> 0%',
            'limit': 'of the values are infinite.',
            'fixes': [],
            'sources': [],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Skewed',
            'meaning': 'The values of a numeric column lean to one side. The alert value is the ' ~ ext('https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skewness', 'skewness') ~ '.',
            'threshold': '|skew| > 2',
            'limit': 'The skewness, without the sign.',
            'fixes': [
              ['You use a linear model, a neural network, a support vector machine, or nearest neighbors', 'Transform the column. The long tail can dominate the fit. Fit the transform on the train data only.'],
              ['You use a tree model', 'Skip the transform. Trees are not affected by skew.'],
              ['Values are positive', 'Use log(1 + x), also called log1p. It also accepts zeros.'],
              ['Some values are negative', 'Use the Yeo-Johnson power transform. Box-Cox needs strictly positive values.'],
              ['A few extreme values cause the skew', 'Open the Outliers section first. Fix a data error at its source.'],
              ['You are not sure', 'Compare the score with and without the transform. A transform does not always improve the model.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kuhn and Johnson, chapter 6', fes ~ '06-Engineering_Numeric_Predictors.html'],
              ['Box and Cox, 1964', 'https://doi.org/10.1111/j.2517-6161.1964.tb00553.x'],
              ['Yeo and Johnson, 2000', 'https://doi.org/10.1093/biomet/87.4.954'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Imbalanced',
            'meaning': 'One value fills most of a column.',
            'threshold': '> 90%',
            'limit': 'of the column is one value.',
            'fixes': [
              ['About 99% of the rows share one value', 'Expect little information in the column. Test its link to the target before you drop it.'],
              ['A rare value marks the event that you want to predict, such as fraud', 'Keep the column. The rare value can be the signal.'],
              ['A category column has rare levels', 'Pool the rare levels into Other.'],
              ['A rare level can vanish in a split', 'Pool the level, or make sure that each split has it. A split without the level creates an empty column.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kuhn and Johnson, chapter 5', fes ~ '05-Encoding_Categorical_Predictors.html'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'High Correlation',
            'meaning': 'Two columns change together. The alert value is the correlation.',
            'threshold': '|r| > 0.8',
            'limit': 'The correlation, without the sign.',
            'fixes': [
              ['You use linear regression or a neural network', 'Keep one column of the pair. Highly correlated columns hurt these models.'],
              ['You read feature importance', 'Group the correlated columns and keep one from each group. Correlated columns share their importance, so each one looks weak.'],
              ['Many columns move together', 'Combine them with principal component analysis (PCA).'],
              ['One column links more closely to the target', 'Keep that column.'],
              ['A very sparse column is in the pair', 'Few values can create a link by chance. Do not rely on the correlation.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kuhn and Johnson, chapter 6', fes ~ '06-Engineering_Numeric_Predictors.html'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Uniform',
            'meaning': 'The values of a column look ' ~ ext('https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discrete_uniform_distribution', 'evenly spread') ~ '. The alert value is a p-value.',
            'threshold': 'p > 0.05',
            'limit': 'The p-value of the test for an even spread.',
            'fixes': [
              ['Column has few values', 'The test is not valid for small samples. Each bin needs an expected count of at least 5. Look at the missing values first.'],
              ['You want to confirm the spread', 'Open the chart in Column Details. A flat histogram confirms it.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['NIST handbook: chi-square test', 'https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/eda/section3/eda35f.htm'],
              ['ASA statement on p-values', 'https://doi.org/10.1080/00031305.2016.1154108'],
            ],
          },
          {
            'name': 'Target Leakage',
            'meaning': 'A column links so closely to the target that it can hold the answer. The alert value is Phi K. This alert needs a target.',
            'threshold': 'Phi K ≥ 0.95',
            'limit': 'The link between the column and the target.',
            'fixes': [
              ['Value is known only after the outcome', 'Drop the column. The model cannot use it when it predicts new cases.'],
              ['Column is a copy or a proxy of the target', 'Drop it. A proxy for the outcome gives the answer away.'],
              ['Link is real and known in advance', 'Keep it. You can use a strong link when you know the value at prediction time. Look at how the value is recorded.'],
              ['You prepared the data before the split', 'Fit scalers, encoders, and selectors on the train data only. Use a pipeline, so that each fold stays clean.'],
              ['Rows have a time order', 'Split by time. Train on the past and test on the future.'],
            ],
            'sources': [
              ['Kapoor and Narayanan, 2023', 'https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patter.2023.100804'],
              ['Kaufman and others, 2012', 'https://doi.org/10.1145/2382577.2382579'],
            ],
          },
        ] %}
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="guide-text">An alert marks a possible problem. The limit decides when the report raises the alert. Open an alert to see its limit, some possible fixes, and the sources behind them. The Feedback tab lists the limits that this report used.</p>
          <p class="guide-text">The advice uses three terms. To impute a value is to fill a gap with an estimate. A flag is a new column that holds 1 where a condition is true and 0 everywhere else. The train data is the part of the data that fits the model.</p>
          <div class="alert-list">
            {% for alert in guide_alerts %}
            <details class="alert-row"{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
              <summary class="alert-summary">
                <span class="alert-chevron">{{ icon('chevron-down', 14) }}</span>
                <span class="alert-term">{{ alert.name }}</span>
                <span class="alert-meaning">{{ alert.meaning }}</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="alert-body">
                <div class="alert-limit">
                  <span class="alert-label">Raised when</span>
                  <span class="alert-limit-value"><code class="alert-threshold">{{ alert.threshold }}</code> {{ alert.limit }}</span>
                </div>
                {% if alert.fixes %}
                <div class="alert-fixes">
                  <h3 class="alert-label">Possible fix</h3>
                  <ol class="fix-steps">
                    {% for when, then in alert.fixes %}
                    <li class="fix-step"><span class="fix-when">{{ when }}</span><span class="fix-then">{{ then }}</span></li>
                    {% endfor %}
                  </ol>
                </div>
                {% else %}
                <div class="alert-limit">
                  <span class="alert-label">Possible fix</span>
                  <span class="alert-limit-value">None with a source yet.</span>
                </div>
                {% endif %}
                <div class="alert-limit">
                  <span class="alert-label">Sources</span>
                  <span class="alert-limit-value">{% for label, url in alert.sources %}{{ ext(url, label) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% else %}None yet.{% endfor %}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </details>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
          <p class="guide-text">A {{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P-value", "p-value") }} is the chance that a pattern appears by luck. A high p-value means that the test cannot rule out an even spread.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-guide-correlations" id="guide-correlations">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-guide-correlations">{{ icon('grid-3x3') }}Correlation methods</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="guide-text">A {{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Correlation", "correlation") }} is a number that shows how closely two columns change together. A value near 0 means no link. A value near 1 means a strong link. The tabs run from the most useful method to the least useful method. A matrix with more than {{ heatmap_limit }} columns shows its strongest pairs and no heatmap. On a narrow screen, such as a phone, the limit is {{ heatmap_mobile_limit }} columns.</p>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="table guide-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>What it measures</th><th>Range</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">{{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearson_correlation_coefficient", "Pearson") }}</td><td>The straight-line link between two numeric columns.</td><td>-1 to 1</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">{{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spearman%27s_rank_correlation_coefficient", "Spearman") }}</td><td>The link between the rank order of two numeric columns. It also finds curves that only rise or only fall.</td><td>-1 to 1</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">{{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kendall_rank_correlation_coefficient", "Kendall") }}</td><td>Like Spearman, but it compares pairs of rows. It works well on small data. With more than 10,000 rows, it uses a random sample of 10,000 rows. The report skips it when the data has more than 50 numeric columns.</td><td>-1 to 1</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">{{ ext("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cram%C3%A9r%27s_V", "Cramers V") }}</td><td>The link between two category columns.</td><td>0 to 1</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">{{ ext("https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.11440", "Phik") }}</td><td>The link between any two columns, numeric or category.</td><td>0 to 1</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="guide-text">For Pearson, Spearman, and Kendall, a negative value means that one column rises when the other column falls.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <div role="tabpanel" id="page-feedback" aria-labelledby="tab-page-feedback" class="space-y-6" hidden>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-feature" id="feature-section">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-feature">{{ icon('lightbulb') }}Request a feature</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="guide-text">Missing something? Ask for it on GitHub. Say what you need and why you need it.</p>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose Open feature request. The link opens a new issue with the template filled in.</li>
            <li>Describe the problem that you want to solve.</li>
            <li>Show how you would like to use the feature. A short code example helps.</li>
            <li>Name any other way that you considered.</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="export-actions">
            <a class="button" href="{{ feature_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ icon('external-link', 14) }}<span>Open feature request</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-problem" id="problem-section">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-problem">{{ icon('bug') }}Report a problem</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="guide-text">Something looks wrong? Tell us on GitHub. A complete report helps us find the cause fast.</p>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose Open GitHub issue. The link opens a new issue with the first part filled in.</li>
            <li>Describe what you did, what you expected, and what happened.</li>
            <li>Choose Copy details in the Reproduction Details section below.</li>
            <li>Paste the copied details at the end of the issue.</li>
          </ol>
          <div class="export-actions">
            <a class="button" href="{{ issue_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ icon('external-link', 14) }}<span>Open GitHub issue</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-reproduction" id="reproduction-section">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-reproduction">{{ icon('settings') }}Reproduction Details</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="code-bar">
            <span class="code-bar-label">Details for the issue</span>
            <button type="button" class="button" data-copy-target="reproduction-text">
              <span class="copy-idle">{{ icon('copy', 14) }}</span>
              <span class="copy-done" hidden>{{ icon('check', 14) }}</span>
              <span class="copy-label">Copy details</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <pre class="code-block" id="reproduction-text">{% set ns = namespace(group='') %}{% for key, val in overview.reproduction.items() %}{% set group = key.split('.')[0] if '.' in key else 'general' %}{% if loop.index0 and group != ns.group %}{{ "\n" }}{% endif %}{% set ns.group = group %}{{ key }}: {{ val }}{{ "\n" }}{% endfor %}{{ "\n" }}rows: {{ overview.n_rows }}{{ "\n" }}columns: {{ overview.n_columns }}{{ "\n" }}column_types: {% for type_name, count in overview.type_distribution.items() %}{{ type_name | lower }}={{ count }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{{ "\n" }}alerts: {% if alerts %}{% for group in alerts | groupby('alert_type') %}{{ group.grouper | lower }}={{ group.list | length }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}none{% endif %}{{ "\n" }}<span id="diagnostic-ui"></span></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sec-about" id="about-section">
        <h2 class="section-title" id="sec-about">{{ icon('info') }}About</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="table guide-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Package</td><td>{{ package_name }}</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Version</td><td>{{ version }}</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="guide-term">Report created</td><td>{{ generated_at }}</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <script>
    (function () {
      function select(tab) {
        var tabs = tab.closest('[role="tablist"]').querySelectorAll('[role="tab"]');
        tabs.forEach(function (t) {
          var on = t === tab;
          t.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(on));
          t.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
          document.getElementById(t.getAttribute('aria-controls')).hidden = !on;
        });
        if (tab.closest('#page-tabs')) {
          window.scrollTo(0, 0);
        }
        document.dispatchEvent(new Event('reportshown'));
        if (!window.echarts) return;
        var panel = document.getElementById(tab.getAttribute('aria-controls'));
        reportTheme.flush(panel);
        panel
          .querySelectorAll('[_echarts_instance_]')
          .forEach(function (el) {
            var chart = echarts.getInstanceByDom(el);
            if (chart) chart.resize();
          });
      }

      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var tab = e.target.closest('[role="tab"]');
        if (tab) select(tab);
      });

      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        var tab = e.target.closest('[role="tab"]');
        if (!tab) return;
        var tabs = Array.prototype.slice.call(
          tab.closest('[role="tablist"]').querySelectorAll('[role="tab"]')
        ).filter(function (t) { return !t.hidden; });
        var i = tabs.indexOf(tab);
        var next = {
          ArrowRight: i + 1, ArrowDown: i + 1, ArrowLeft: i - 1, ArrowUp: i - 1,
          Home: 0, End: tabs.length - 1
        }[e.key];
        if (next === undefined) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        var target = tabs[(next + tabs.length) % tabs.length];
        target.focus();
        select(target);
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-layout-choice]').forEach(function (choice) {
        choice.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var target = document.getElementById(choice.dataset.layoutTarget);
          var layout = choice.dataset.layoutChoice;
          target.dataset.layout = layout;
          var tablist = target.querySelector('[aria-orientation]');
          if (tablist) {
            tablist.setAttribute('aria-orientation', layout === 'list' ? 'vertical' : 'horizontal');
          }
          choice.parentNode.querySelectorAll('[data-layout-choice]').forEach(function (other) {
            other.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(other === choice));
          });
          target.querySelectorAll('[data-layout-show]').forEach(function (el) {
            el.hidden = el.dataset.layoutShow !== layout;
          });
          if (!window.echarts) return;
          reportTheme.flush(target);
          target.querySelectorAll('[_echarts_instance_]').forEach(function (el) {
            var chart = echarts.getInstanceByDom(el);
            if (chart && el.offsetWidth) chart.resize();
          });
        });
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-truncate-target]').forEach(function (button) {
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var on = button.getAttribute('aria-pressed') !== 'true';
          button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(on));
          button.title = 'Compact cells: ' + (on ? 'on' : 'off');
          button.querySelector('.truncate-on').hidden = !on;
          button.querySelector('.truncate-off').hidden = on;
          document.getElementById(button.dataset.truncateTarget).dataset.truncate = on ? 'on' : 'off';
        });
      });

      function legacyCopy(text) {
        var area = document.createElement('textarea');
        area.value = text;
        area.setAttribute('readonly', '');
        area.style.position = 'fixed';
        area.style.opacity = '0';
        document.body.appendChild(area);
        area.select();
        var copied = false;
        try { copied = document.execCommand('copy'); } catch (err) { copied = false; }
        document.body.removeChild(area);
        return copied;
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy-target]').forEach(function (button) {
        var idle = button.querySelector('.copy-idle');
        var done = button.querySelector('.copy-done');
        var label = button.querySelector('.copy-label');

        function markCopied() {
          idle.hidden = true;
          done.hidden = false;
          label.textContent = 'Copied';
          setTimeout(function () {
            idle.hidden = false;
            done.hidden = true;
            label.textContent = 'Copy';
          }, 2000);
        }

        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var text = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copyTarget).textContent;
          if (navigator.clipboard) {
            navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(markCopied, function () {
              if (legacyCopy(text)) markCopied();
            });
          } else if (legacyCopy(text)) {
            markCopied();
          }
        });
      });

      var filter = document.getElementById('col-filter');
      filter.addEventListener('input', function () {
        var query = filter.value.trim().toLowerCase();
        var shown = 0;
        document.querySelectorAll('#col-tabs [role="tab"]').forEach(function (tab) {
          var match = tab.title.toLowerCase().indexOf(query) !== -1;
          tab.hidden = !match;
          if (match) shown += 1;
        });
        document.getElementById('col-empty').hidden = shown !== 0;
      });

      var settingsButton = document.getElementById('settings-button');
      var settingsMenu = document.getElementById('settings-menu');
      var settingItems = settingsMenu.querySelectorAll('[data-setting]');

      function syncSettings() {
        settingItems.forEach(function (item) {
          var current = reportSettings.get(item.dataset.setting) === item.dataset.value;
          item.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(current));
        });
      }

      function toggleSettings(open) {
        settingsMenu.hidden = !open;
        settingsButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
      }

      settingsButton.addEventListener('click', function () { toggleSettings(settingsMenu.hidden); });
      settingItems.forEach(function (item) {
        item.addEventListener('click', function () {
          reportSettings.set(item.dataset.setting, item.dataset.value);
          syncSettings();
        });
      });
      document.getElementById('settings-reset').addEventListener('click', function () {
        reportSettings.reset();
        syncSettings();
      });
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var outside = !settingsMenu.contains(e.target) && !settingsButton.contains(e.target);
        if (!settingsMenu.hidden && outside) toggleSettings(false);
      });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key !== 'Escape' || settingsMenu.hidden) return;
        toggleSettings(false);
        settingsButton.focus();
      });
      syncSettings();

      var diagnosticUi = document.getElementById('diagnostic-ui');

      function fillDiagnostics() {
        diagnosticUi.textContent = 'theme: ' + reportSettings.get('theme') + '\n' +
          'density: ' + reportSettings.get('density') + '\n' +
          'viewport: ' + window.innerWidth + 'x' + window.innerHeight + '\n' +
          'browser: ' + navigator.userAgent + '\n';
      }

      fillDiagnostics();
      document.addEventListener('reportshown', fillDiagnostics);

      function saveLink(name, href) {
        var link = document.createElement('a');
        link.href = href;
        link.download = name;
        document.body.appendChild(link);
        link.click();
        document.body.removeChild(link);
      }

      function saveCsv(name, rows) {
        var lines = rows.map(function (row) {
          return row.map(function (cell) {
            return '"' + String(cell).replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
          }).join(',');
        });
        var blob = new Blob(['\uFEFF' + lines.join('\n')], {type: 'text/csv;charset=utf-8'});
        var href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
        saveLink(name + '.csv', href);
        URL.revokeObjectURL(href);
      }

      function fileStem(text) {
        return text.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '') || 'report';
      }

      function chartOf(id) {
        var el = document.getElementById(id);
        return el ? echarts.getInstanceByDom(el) : null;
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-export]').forEach(function (button) {
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var table = document.querySelector('#variables-section table');
          if (!table) return;
          saveCsv('variables', Array.prototype.map.call(table.rows, function (row) {
            return Array.prototype.map.call(row.cells, function (cell) {
              return cell.textContent.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
            });
          }));
        });
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-save-table]').forEach(function (button) {
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var panel = document.getElementById(button.dataset.saveTable);
          var view = panel.querySelector('[role="tabpanel"]:not([hidden])');
          var table = view && view.querySelector('table');
          if (!table) return;
          var rows = Array.prototype.map.call(table.rows, function (row) {
            return Array.prototype.map.call(row.cells, function (cell) {
              if (cell.tagName === 'TH') return cell.title;
              return cell.querySelector('.muted') ? '' : cell.title;
            });
          });
          saveCsv(view.id.replace(/^panel-/, ''), rows);
        });
      });

      function saveMatrix(id, name) {
        var chart = chartOf(id);
        if (!chart) return;
        var labels = chart.getOption().xAxis[0].data;
        var rows = labels.map(function (label) {
          return [label].concat(labels.map(function () { return ''; }));
        });
        chart.getOption().series[0].data.forEach(function (item) {
          var cell = item.value || item;
          if (cell[2] !== null && !isNaN(cell[2])) rows[cell[1]][cell[0] + 1] = cell[2];
        });
        saveCsv(name, [[''].concat(labels)].concat(rows));
      }

      function savePng(id, name) {
        var chart = chartOf(id);
        if (!chart) return;
        var href = chart.getDataURL({type: 'png', pixelRatio: 2, backgroundColor: reportTheme.token('editor')});
        saveLink(fileStem(name) + '.png', href);
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-save-png]').forEach(function (button) {
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var name = button.dataset.name;
          if (button.dataset.nameFrom) {
            name = button.dataset.nameFrom.split(',').map(function (id) {
              return document.getElementById(id).value;
            }).join(' vs ');
          }
          savePng(button.dataset.savePng, name);
        });
      });

      var corrTools = document.getElementById('corr-tools');
      var narrowScreen = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 40rem)');

      function shownHeatmap() {
        var panel = document.querySelector('#correlations-section [role="tabpanel"]:not([hidden])');
        if (!panel || !panel.dataset.heatmap) return null;
        if (narrowScreen.matches && 'mobileHidden' in panel.dataset) return null;
        return panel;
      }

      function syncCorrelationTools() {
        if (corrTools) corrTools.hidden = !shownHeatmap();
      }

      if (corrTools) {
        document.getElementById('corr-save-csv').addEventListener('click', function () {
          var panel = shownHeatmap();
          if (panel) saveMatrix(panel.dataset.heatmap, panel.dataset.name);
        });
        document.getElementById('corr-save-png').addEventListener('click', function () {
          var panel = shownHeatmap();
          if (panel) savePng(panel.dataset.heatmap, panel.dataset.name);
        });
        document.addEventListener('reportshown', syncCorrelationTools);
        narrowScreen.addEventListener('change', syncCorrelationTools);
        syncCorrelationTools();
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-chart-id]').forEach(function (tab) {
        tab.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var panel = tab.closest('[id^="panel-col-"]');
          var save = panel && panel.querySelector('[data-save-png]');
          if (!save) return;
          save.dataset.savePng = tab.dataset.chartId;
          save.dataset.name = tab.dataset.chartName;
        });
      });

      (function () {
        var detail = document.querySelector('.columns-detail');
        if (!detail) return;
        var rows = 0;
        detail.querySelectorAll('table.table-dense').forEach(function (table) {
          rows = Math.max(rows, table.rows.length);
        });
        detail.style.setProperty('--detail-rows', String(rows));
      })();

      function applyLimit(box) {
        var limit = parseInt(box.dataset.limit, 10);
        var open = box.dataset.expanded === 'true';
        var items = Array.prototype.filter.call(box.children, function (child) {
          return !child.hasAttribute('data-limit-skip');
        });
        items.forEach(function (item, index) { item.hidden = !open && index >= limit; });
        var button = document.querySelector('[data-limit-toggle="' + box.id + '"]');
        if (!button) return;
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
        button.querySelector('.more-label').textContent =
          open ? 'Show less' : 'Show ' + (items.length - limit) + ' more';
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-limit]').forEach(function (box) {
        applyLimit(box);
        var toggle = document.querySelector('[data-limit-toggle="' + box.id + '"]');
        if (!toggle) return;
        toggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
          box.dataset.expanded = String(box.dataset.expanded !== 'true');
          applyLimit(box);
        });
      });

      window.matchMedia('(max-width: 40rem)').addEventListener('change', function () {
        reportTheme.flush();
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-sortable]').forEach(function (table) {
        var body = table.tBodies[0];
        var heads = table.querySelectorAll('th');
        heads.forEach(function (head, col) {
          var button = head.querySelector('.sort-button');
          if (!button) return;
          button.addEventListener('click', function () {
            var ascending = head.getAttribute('aria-sort') !== 'ascending';
            var numeric = button.dataset.sortType === 'num';
            heads.forEach(function (other) { other.setAttribute('aria-sort', 'none'); });
            head.setAttribute('aria-sort', ascending ? 'ascending' : 'descending');
            var rows = Array.prototype.slice.call(body.rows);
            rows.sort(function (a, b) {
              var x = a.cells[col].dataset.value;
              var y = b.cells[col].dataset.value;
              var blankX = x === undefined || x === '';
              var blankY = y === undefined || y === '';
              if (blankX || blankY) return blankX === blankY ? 0 : (blankX ? 1 : -1);
              var diff = numeric ? parseFloat(x) - parseFloat(y) : x.localeCompare(y);
              return ascending ? diff : -diff;
            });
            rows.forEach(function (row) { body.appendChild(row); });
            if (body.dataset.limit) applyLimit(body);
          });
        });
      });

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-column]').forEach(function (link) {
        link.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var tab = document.getElementById('tab-col-' + link.dataset.openColumn);
          if (!tab) return;
          if (tab.hidden) {
            filter.value = '';
            filter.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));
          }
          select(tab);
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>

  <script>
    (function () {
      var areas = document.querySelectorAll('.chip-list, .menu');

      function mark(area) {
        area.toggleAttribute('data-scrolls', area.scrollHeight - area.clientHeight > 1);
      }

      var observer = new ResizeObserver(function (entries) {
        entries.forEach(function (entry) { mark(entry.target); });
      });
      areas.forEach(function (area) {
        observer.observe(area);
        mark(area);
      });
      document.addEventListener('reportshown', function () { areas.forEach(mark); });
    })();
  </script>

  <script>
    (function () {
      var frame = null;
      try { frame = window.frameElement; } catch (err) { return; }
      if (!frame || String(frame.getAttribute('onload')).indexOf('__resizeIframe') === -1) return;

      function fit() {
        var height = document.body.offsetHeight;
        if (height > 0 && frame.style.height !== height + 'px') frame.style.height = height + 'px';
      }

      fit();
      document.addEventListener('reportshown', fit);
      new ResizeObserver(fit).observe(document.body);
    })();
  </script>

</body>
</html>
